WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.659
Speaker 1: We have to talk about books.

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:03.830
I like books.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.290
I like reading and I say more books to the
better.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.450
As a general rule doesn't mean every book
is appropriate for every setting or every

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:12.450
situation.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:17.320
OK, we've talked about that before, but the
real question I have is, according to these

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.929
right wingers, is banning books good or bad.

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:26.369
And you might be saying, Well, David, no,
it's obviously good or it's obviously bad,

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:33.510
but it's really not so clear because we see
both perspectives from this modern American

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:39.120
book burning contingent that exists in the
right.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.980
As I talk to you about not that long ago,
book banned efforts have hit their highest

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.910
levels and at least 20 years.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.039
And it's the right, not the left, that's doing.

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:54.060
As we looked at this article must have been
what is this article even from about a month

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.060
ago?

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.339
We look we did the story a couple of weeks
ago, three three weeks ago or so that book

00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:03.489
band efforts led by the American right wing
are at their highest level in 20 years now.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:07.660
What we mean by book bands differs in different
situations.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.500
In some cases, what we're talking about is
a movement by the right to ban a book from

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.300
being used in school.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.060
Sometimes it's novels.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.800
Sometimes it's certain history books, etc.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.550
They're not necessarily calling for the books
to not be published or for the books to be

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.400
against the law.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.320
But they certainly want to cancel a teacher's
ability to say, Here's a book that I want

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.320
to teach from.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.600
They don't want to give teachers that opportunity.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.430
In other cases, it's confusion about what
it even means, and we're going to get to that

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.430
in a moment.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:48.560
But we know that the efforts to ban books
are at multi-decade highs led by the American

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.010
right wing, so they must be in favor of the
book bands, right?

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:59.240
Well, apparently not, because remember the
Dr. Seuss situation?

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.350
This was now about a year ago.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:07.140
It's actually hard to believe it's been a
year, but it has been a year where the publisher

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:10.979
of Dr. Seuss Books said, Hey, you know what?

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:11.979
Some of these books.

00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:13.030
This is our review.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.710
We're a private business.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.400
We can make the decisions that are right for
us.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:24.910
We believe that some of these Dr. Seuss books,
they have elements that are not really sensitive

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.900
to modern cultural sensitivities.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:28.900
We're a private business.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.510
We're a publisher, and we think it's not good
for business to keep publishing some of these.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.150
So we're not going to keep printing more copies.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.790
We're not burning the books.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.260
We're not saying the books should be against
the law.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.930
We're not saying people can't read them.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.610
We just think continuing to print these particular
books is no longer in line with what's best

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:46.630
for us.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:52.610
And the right went crazy, saying, Oh my God,
the the left is banning the books.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.130
They're canceling Dr. Seuss.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.180
It's terrible.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.430
Always allow the books everywhere, everywhere,
everywhere.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.430
Oh, OK.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.390
So they're against, I guess, limitations on
books.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:06.940
Except now, as we talked about yesterday.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:12.090
And as we've been talking about for several
months, they seem fine banning books when

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:18.260
it's books that they don't like, when it's
history books that tell the real story.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:25.620
As far as we know at this time of slavery,
of racial discrimination, of all sorts of

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.170
different aspects of history.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.180
All of a sudden, the very same right wingers
who were saying they're canceling Dr. Seuss,

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.230
they say, We got to get these books the hell
out of here.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:44.470
We now are learning about this new effort
in Florida to reject math textbooks because

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.060
they contain so-called critical race theory.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:53.980
Although Ron DeSantis and other Floridians
have not been able to provide a single substantive

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.330
example of where such critical race theory
exists.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:02.630
So I guess the question of is banning books
good or bad?

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.280
The answer is, well, I guess it depends on
their mood.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.830
I guess it depends on which books.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.130
I guess it depends on who's doing it and why.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:15.349
And it's a very similar phenomenon with protests.

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:20.910
If you're protesting police brutality, if
you're protesting in favor of Black Lives

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.860
Matter, if you're protesting in defense of
George Floyd.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.159
Well, then these protests are dangerous to
law enforcement and we've got a back the blue

00:04:30.159 --> 00:04:34.419
and they're all violent and looting and all
these different things.

00:04:34.419 --> 00:04:41.240
But if you're protesting against Joe Biden
being the president and getting sworn in because

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.960
he was elected on January six, well, then
you're doing the right thing and you're being

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.349
treated very unfairly by everybody.

00:04:48.349 --> 00:04:49.550
And what about back the blue?

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:50.729
Because they beat up some cops?

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:51.729
Oh no, no, no.

00:04:51.729 --> 00:04:55.639
We don't care about that all of a sudden because
they were protesting against the certification

00:04:55.639 --> 00:04:56.639
of the election.

00:04:56.639 --> 00:04:58.860
Oh, so I guess it's not really so simple.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:05.129
And the principle here is the one I've been
telling you about now for years, which is

00:05:05.129 --> 00:05:09.150
they don't even really care about their own
stated principles.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:17.319
They stake out apparent principles to justify
the end results that they already want.

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:23.259
If their principles all of a sudden would
point to actually Black Lives Matter can protest.

00:05:23.259 --> 00:05:26.669
Actually, you shouldn't ban these books.

00:05:26.669 --> 00:05:30.669
Then they change their principles because
their principles are no longer convenient

00:05:30.669 --> 00:05:32.469
to their preexisting end goals.

00:05:32.469 --> 00:05:36.440
And this is the theme we've been following
for years at this point in time.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.379
I don't think this is going to stop anytime
soon, and in particular because they don't

00:05:40.379 --> 00:05:45.539
really want to engage on what should climate
policy be, what should policy be on renewable

00:05:45.539 --> 00:05:46.880
sources of energy?

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.659
What should the top tax rate be?

00:05:48.659 --> 00:05:50.659
They can only engage completely.

00:05:50.659 --> 00:05:53.449
Superficially, taxes are bad.

00:05:53.449 --> 00:05:58.689
Green New Deal is bad because they are unwilling
or unable to engage substantively on those

00:05:58.689 --> 00:05:59.689
issues.

00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:01.969
They're going to keep pushing this stuff and
it works.

00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:06.449
I don't want to be a broken record, but part
of why Glenn Youngkin won the Virginia gubernatorial

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:08.639
race is because this stuff works.

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:10.870
I will ban teaching of critical race theory.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:11.870
Who's teaching it?

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:12.870
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:13.870
I will ban it.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:14.870
Wow, I'm going to vote for this guy.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.430
This stuff works.

